SUMMARY:AMOS After Hours: Conspiracies\, Urban Legends\, Local Lore
DESCRIPTION:AMOS 21+ night is back with our Halloween After Hours!\nBuy Tickets Now\n\nThis Halloween season are you ready to step into the world of conspiracy theories\, local lore\, and urban legends? \nJoin our community of science experts\, storytellers\, artists\, and folklorists as we bunk or debunk some of history’s greatest mysteries. What do YOU want to believe? \nThis year we’re adding a little treat to your tricks- spooky onigiri from Nibbly Onigiri and specialty themed cocktails. \nMeet our Lucky 13 Lineup: \nKatie Ybarra\, Montford Park Players- Tinfoil Hat Contest (The Rules: you can bring one from home or make one at AMOS. Must use enough tinfoil to protect head from mind control. Judging is at 8pm and 1st place prize is two tickets to our Under the Stars party). \nNOAA- Cloud Seeding and Weather Modification \nFeminist Bird Club- Are Birds Real? \nOut of the Woods Therapy- Your Brain on Conspiracies \nBeth Frith- Chocolate Ensh*ttification Lab (experiments to tell if our candy is getting worse) \nShara Crosby (@birth.mark tattoo)- Taylor Swift Easter Egg Temporary Tattoos (are you a swifty\, a gaylor\, an artler\, or a hater? Choose your conspiracy) \nKate Whittier- The Moon Landing and Space Secrets \nRemix It! AVL- Is Recycling a Conspiracy? \nElla Parker\, AMOS- Broom Making Workshop (brooms! Cultural symbol\, tool\, gravitational anomaly? Make your own to take home!) \nJJ Frid\, WCU Forensic Osteology- Tales from the Crypt (the true story of restoring Riverside Cemetery’s gravesites after Helene) \nAMOS- The Brown Mountain Lights \nUNCA + Minerals Research Lab- Quartz and the Asheville Vortex \nThe Science of Appalachian Granny Witches \n————————————————————————— \n\n\nCostumes are encouraged but cannot include masks that cover the entire face\, weapons\, or weapon-like objects. \nPre-registration is strongly recommended. Tickets are $25 online*.  \nMust be 21+\, your admission includes one free drink.  \n*AMOS has a limited amount of income-based discounted tickets for $15. If you would like to reserve a sliding scale ticket please email redacted@example.invalid.
URL:https://ashevillescience.org/event/amos-after-hours/
LOCATION:Asheville Museum of Science\, 43 Patton Ave\, Asheville\, NC\, 28801\, United States
CATEGORIES:After Hours Events
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://ashevillescience.org/wp-content/uploads/websiteHWafterhours.jpg
